gpsim 0.31.0: ADDWF on POSTINCn/POSTDECn/PREINCn with d=W never updates FSR.

ADDWF16::execute() reads its operand with get_value(), which bypasses the
indirect-register side effects. With d=F the following put() still adjusts
FSR, but `ADDWF POSTINC0, W` leaves FSR0 unchanged, unlike real PIC18 hardware
and unlike SUBWF/IORWF/ANDWF/ADDWFC. Use get(), as SUBWF16 does;
Indirect_Addressing applies at most one FSR update per instruction cycle, so
the d=F read-modify-write still increments once.

--- a/src/16bit-instructions.cc
+++ b/src/16bit-instructions.cc
@@ -393,7 +393,7 @@
     source = cpu_pic->registers[register_address];
   }

-  new_value = (src_value = source->get_value()) + (w_value = cpu16->Wget());
+  new_value = (src_value = source->get()) + (w_value = cpu16->Wget());

   // Store the result

